## Group 3: Learning the Rules to Break Them

<img src="https://c.tenor.com/7ctSMF73xMMAAAAd/tenor.gif" height=100% width=100%>

Your group explores how the KLF systematically studied the conventions of every genre they entered before subverting or abandoning them — and what that sequence tells us about how genre mastery and disruption work together.

*Why this matters*: Your MA2 literacy practice has conventions — rules, expectations, norms that practitioners learn, often without being explicitly taught. Identifying them is the analytical work the assignment asks you to do.

### Your Pathway

1. **Discussion 1**: How did the KLF's apprenticeship model shape their ability to disrupt? Do you see any examples of this in contemporary culture?

2. **Discussion 2**: What conventions currently govern your work toward MA2 — what might it mean to break them in MA3?

3. **Shareout Prep**: Organize your findings to share with the class.

